From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] setupapi, cfgmgr32: implement the device and class stubs

setupapi, cfgmgr32: implement the device and class stubs

These setupapi and cfgmgr32 entry points returned ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED
or CR_FAILURE. Installers and device tools call them and then give up.

Implemented:
- CM_Connect_MachineA/W and CM_Disconnect_Machine: local machine only (NULL,
  "" or this computer's \\name); a remote name fails with
  CR_REMOTE_COMM_FAILURE, a malformed one with CR_INVALID_MACHINENAME.
- CM_Enumerate_Classes and _Ex: installer classes from Control\Class and
  interface classes from Control\DeviceClasses; CR_NO_SUCH_VALUE past the end.
- CM_Get/Set_Class_Registry_PropertyA/W and SetupDiGet/SetClassRegistry-
  PropertyA/W: upper and lower filters, security (SDDL in, binary out),
  device type, exclusivity and characteristics, with the documented
  CR_* / ERROR_* mapping. The CM_Get_Class_Registry_Property spec signature
  is corrected.
- SetupDiGetSelectedDevice / SetupDiSetSelectedDevice.
- SetupDiDestroyDriverInfoList: really frees the list and the selection.
- CM_Get_DevNode_Registry_Property_ExA.
- SetupDiGetCustomDevicePropertyA/W, including DICUSTOMDEVPROP_MERGE_MULTISZ.
- SetupQueryInfVersionInformationA/W.

include/cfgmgr32.h gains the matching prototypes and flags.

Gate: test/setupcm-gate.sh.
